// N114-hc: hyper-connection (GatedResidual) decode kernels for Intel Xe2 (Arc Pro B70) as a torch XPU op library
// (torch.ops.n114hc.*). Qwen3.8-Flash-Next decode / verify: M = 1..8 token rows share the weights, which are read ONCE
// for all rows (6.6 MB Wd + 6.6 MB Wu + 80 KB Wi per call at hc 4, hidden 2560, lowrank 320).
//
// Port of Strata's fused hyper-connection read (sycl/src/kernels/cuda/fused_gr.dp.cpp + include/strata/kernels/
// fused_gr.hpp of github.com/Niko1221/Strata, HEAD 82f46a8: fused_gr_read / fused_gr_read_multi, "the HC read in two
// kernels with the previous half's write folded in", split-K down partials summed in a fixed order by the up kernel).
// Adapted to SGLang's GatedResidual (layers/hyperconnection.py, compiled _mix_compute / _combine_compute) and its
// bf16 activations and rounding points (Strata keeps R and the activations in fp32):
//   norm     n   = bf16( (x * rsqrt(sum_g(x^2) / hs + eps)) * (1 + w) )         per (row, branch g of hs columns)
//   down     t   = bf16( n . Wd[k] )            k < lowrank      (F.linear, fp32 accumulation)
//            a   = bf16( silu(t / hc) )                          (inductor: one rounding)
//   up       u   = bf16( a . Wu[r] )            r < hc*hs        (F.linear)
//            mix = bf16( (sum_j sigmoid(u[j*hs+d]) * n[j*hs+d]) / hc )
//   inject   l   = bf16( n . Wi[j] )            j < hc           (computed with the down rows, used by combine)
//   combine  g   = bf16( 2 * sigmoid(l / hc) ),  out = bf16( R + bo * g )
// Kernels (each launch reads the weights once for all M rows):
//   pre      one work-group per (row, branch): [optional fold of the previous half's combine: R' = combine(R, bo, l),
//            written as the new residual] + rsqrt of the branch + n (bf16) written          grid M*hc x (hs/8)
//   down     (16-row block, K split): stages its K slice of n for all M rows in SLM, one sub-group per weight row,
//            fp32 partial dots -> part[split][m][row]  (Wd rows then Wi rows)               grid ceil(R/16)*KS x 256
//   up       (UC output columns): sums the KS partials in a fixed order -> a (SLM); every Wu row read once (one
//            lane per row, or one sub-group per row), u rounded, sigmoid * n, mean over the hc branches -> mix;
//            work-group 0 also writes l = bf16(sum of the Wi partials)                       grid hs/UC x UC*hc
//   combine  elementwise R + bo * g (the non-folded combine)
// No host syncs, no host reads of device data, allocations only through at::empty: XPU-graph capturable.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
